cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Applied Geostatistics in Python: A Hands-on Guide with GeostatsPy"
message: >
  If you use this book, software, or educational materials in your
  research or teaching, please cite the specific release version using the
  metadata below.
type: book

authors:
  - family-names: "Pyrcz"
    given-names: "Michael J."
    affiliation: "The University of Texas at Austin"
    orcid: "0000-0002-5983-219X"

abstract: >
  An open-source, hands-on guide to applied geostatistics using Python and
  GeostatsPy. The book integrates theory with practical, reproducible workflows
  and interactive Jupyter notebooks. Topics include probability, spatial data
  analysis, variogram modeling, kriging, stochastic simulation, uncertainty
  quantification, and machine learning applications in subsurface
  characterization. Supporting materials include a comprehensive glossary,
  YouTube lecture series, GitHub repositories, and interactive computational
  dashboards.

